  "discrepancies": [
    {
      "kind": "missing_from_ui",
      "options": [
        "quit_app_on_disconnect",
        "virtual_display",
        "clipboard_sync",
        "web_ui_enabled"
      ],
      "detail": "Parsed by config.cpp apply_config() but absent from config.html tabs[].options and every .vue file (zero occurrences anywhere under src_assets/common/assets/web/). Only reachable today by hand-editing sunshine.conf. tab/default assigned here from config.cpp struct initializers (config.cpp:437-587), not from UI. clipboard_sync and web_ui_enabled were added to the schema without a UI control on purpose: web_ui_enabled gates the confighttp listener that serves this very UI (self-disabling via the UI it disables would be a footgun), and clipboard_sync mirrors that config-file-only reach until/unless a control is deliberately added."
    },
    {
      "kind": "hidden_on_macos",
      "options": [
        "capture",
        "gamepad",
        "qp"
      ],
      "detail": "Present in config.html tabs[].options (cross-platform default bag) but the .vue control is unconditionally hidden when platform === 'macos' (Advanced.vue v-if=\"platform !== 'macos'\" for capture and qp; Inputs.vue v-if=\"... && platform !== 'macos'\" for gamepad). On this macOS-only fork these options are parsed and defaulted but never user-editable via the web UI. qp is additionally dead code on this fork: config::video.qp (src/config.h:25, parsed src/config.cpp:1073) is never read by any encoder path, macOS or otherwise -- the UI hide just stops surfacing a control with zero effect."
    },
    {
      "kind": "unconstrained_parser_vs_ui_enum",
      "options": [
        "amd_quality",
        "amd_rc",
        "amd_usage",
        "capture",
        "encoder",
        "sw_preset",
        "sw_tune"
      ],
      "detail": "Parser uses string_f (accepts any string, no server-side allow-list) while the corresponding .vue renders a <select> with a fixed hardcoded <option> list. saveConfig() (confighttp.cpp:986) writes any value posted for these keys straight to the config file with zero validation -- this is exactly the '// TODO: Input Validation' gap the design doc calls out. Schema records type=string (parser truth) per these entries; UI-observed enum values are NOT encoded in constraints.enum for these because the parser does not enforce them (would be a false enum-parity signal for the gate)."
    },
    {
      "kind": "opaque_converter_enum",
      "options": [
        "nvenc_twopass",
        "dd_configuration_option",
        "dd_resolution_option",
        "dd_refresh_rate_option",
        "dd_hdr_option",
        "qsv_preset",
        "qsv_coder",
        "amd_coder",
        "vt_coder",
        "vt_realtime",
        "vt_software"
      ],
      "detail": "Parsed via generic_f(...) or the 4-arg int_f(vars,name,var,converter) form. The allowed string set lives in an external *_from_view() converter (e.g. qsv::preset_from_view, dd::config_option_from_view) defined outside config.cpp/config.h, not in a literal allow-list the parser exposes -- so it is outside the regex-reachable 'parser truth' this test can verify. constraints.enum on these entries is sourced from the matching .vue <option> list (UI truth) as best-effort documentation, and the parity test does NOT assert it against config.cpp for this reason (see kind='opaque_converter_enum' -> type/enum parity skipped, name-only parity enforced)."
    },
    {
      "kind": "dynamic_enum",
      "options": [
        "gamepad"
      ],
      "detail": "string_restricted_f's allow-list is get_supported_gamepad_options() (config.cpp:1037), populated at runtime from platf::supported_gamepads(nullptr) -- platform/build dependent, not a static literal. No constraints.enum is recorded; schema type is 'enum' per the string_restricted_f helper but the value set cannot be captured statically. Also see 'hidden_on_macos'."
    },
    {
      "kind": "alias_values_not_in_ui_enum",
      "options": [
        "min_log_level"
      ],
      "detail": "Parser (config.cpp:1285-1310) accepts either a digit '0'-'6' or a word alias (verbose/debug/info/warning/error/fatal/none); General.vue's <select> only ever writes/display the digit form. constraints.enum records the UI-reachable digit strings only; the word aliases are real accepted input but console/API-only."
    }
  ]
}